WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.746 --> 00:00:07.579
It's undeniable

00:00:07.579 --> 00:00:09.832
that the rise of the
UFC has been historic.

00:00:12.406 --> 00:00:13.239
In 20 years,

00:00:13.239 --> 00:00:14.448
the company has taken a sport,

00:00:14.448 --> 00:00:16.064
which was illegal in many states,

00:00:16.064 --> 00:00:18.195
and turned it into an anchor product,

00:00:18.195 --> 00:00:20.110
for the biggest sports
network in the world.

00:00:20.110 --> 00:00:22.253
I don't care what color you are,

00:00:22.253 --> 00:00:23.903
what country you come from,

00:00:23.903 --> 00:00:25.342
or what language you speak.

00:00:25.342 --> 00:00:26.596
We're all human beings.

00:00:26.596 --> 00:00:27.982
And for some reason,

00:00:27.982 --> 00:00:29.531
fighting is in our DNA man.

00:00:29.531 --> 00:00:32.071
At the center of it all is Dana White.

00:00:32.071 --> 00:00:34.195
And he's as big of a
character as you can find.

00:00:34.195 --> 00:00:35.735
Shut the up,

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.219
you scumbag.

00:00:37.219 --> 00:00:39.712
Dana White is the "ID",

00:00:39.712 --> 00:00:41.314
of the UFC in many ways.

00:00:41.314 --> 00:00:43.950
But behind the bluster and hyperbole,

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:46.889
there's a monumental
business story happening.

00:00:46.889 --> 00:00:49.441
'Cause the UFC doesn't
just wanna be mainstream.

00:00:49.441 --> 00:00:52.645
It wants to be the most
popular sport in the world.

00:00:52.645 --> 00:00:55.746
And even that ambition may be too limited.

00:00:58.138 --> 00:00:59.359
Now the crown jewel,

00:00:59.359 --> 00:01:01.492
is super agent Ari
Emanuel's endeavor empire.

00:01:01.492 --> 00:01:03.121
The UFC is influencing,

00:01:03.121 --> 00:01:04.327
not just sports,

00:01:04.327 --> 00:01:05.386
but culture,

00:01:05.386 --> 00:01:06.219
media,

00:01:06.219 --> 00:01:07.279
and entertainment.

00:01:07.279 --> 00:01:08.800
And for them nothing,

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:09.855
not a pandemic or bruising legal fight,

00:01:09.855 --> 00:01:11.750
will stand in their way.

00:01:11.750 --> 00:01:13.646
It's hard for people,

00:01:13.646 --> 00:01:14.903
to really wrap their brains around,

00:01:14.903 --> 00:01:17.032
how big this business can really be.

00:01:17.032 --> 00:01:18.351
But I get it.

00:01:18.351 --> 00:01:20.020
I know what this thing is capable of.

00:01:20.020 --> 00:01:21.487
And I always have.

00:01:39.091 --> 00:01:39.924
To understand,

00:01:39.924 --> 00:01:42.838
one of the most interesting
stories in the world of sports,

00:01:42.838 --> 00:01:46.838
and business you have to
come here to Las Vegas.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:49.276
It's not about betting.

00:01:49.276 --> 00:01:50.860
It's not about the new football team,

00:01:50.860 --> 00:01:53.187
or even the hockey team that
everyone's so excited about.

00:01:53.187 --> 00:01:54.573
It's about one sport,

00:01:54.573 --> 00:01:55.693
the UFC.

00:01:55.693 --> 00:01:56.980
And it's about one guy,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:57.897
Dana White.

00:01:58.978 --> 00:02:00.061
Dana!

00:02:01.959 --> 00:02:02.980
More than 20 years ago,

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.564
White convinced his high school friends,

00:02:04.564 --> 00:02:06.891
Frank and Lorenzo Fertitta
to go in with him,

00:02:06.891 --> 00:02:09.641
on buying the UFC for $2 million.

00:02:14.050 --> 00:02:15.568
Today estimates value the UFC,

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:18.318
at closer to nine or $10 billion.

00:02:21.223 --> 00:02:23.947
It's the centerpiece of
one of the largest talent,

00:02:23.947 --> 00:02:27.246
and entertainment companies in the world.

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.275
And three years into a contract with ESPN,

00:02:29.275 --> 00:02:32.275
the UFC is growing faster than ever.

00:02:34.027 --> 00:02:36.153
But to understand how we
got to this moment in 2021,

00:02:36.153 --> 00:02:38.863
you have to understand
the last two decades,

00:02:38.863 --> 00:02:41.371
and the best person to ask about that,

00:02:41.371 --> 00:02:44.653
is Dana himself in his natural habitat.

00:02:44.653 --> 00:02:45.486
Hey, Dana.

00:02:45.486 --> 00:02:46.501
Crazy how's that?

00:02:46.501 --> 00:02:47.339
Nice to see you.

00:02:47.339 --> 00:02:48.172
You too.

00:02:48.172 --> 00:02:49.271
This is an incredible office.

00:02:49.271 --> 00:02:50.104
Oh thanks.

00:02:50.104 --> 00:02:50.937
By the way.

00:02:50.937 --> 00:02:51.770
Look at,

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:52.603
come over here.

00:02:52.603 --> 00:02:53.436
This is my bar.

00:02:53.436 --> 00:02:54.325
Oh my gosh.

00:02:54.325 --> 00:02:56.741
And this is my gym.

00:02:56.741 --> 00:02:57.713
I'll come in here in the morning.

00:02:57.713 --> 00:02:58.546
I work out,

00:02:58.546 --> 00:02:59.379
shower,

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.212
and then start my day.

00:03:00.212 --> 00:03:01.045
Right.

00:03:03.937 --> 00:03:05.469
As I've dug into this business.

00:03:05.469 --> 00:03:07.509
I mean it's mind blowing,

00:03:07.509 --> 00:03:09.129
I think for anyone
who's looking at it say,

00:03:09.129 --> 00:03:09.962
it's two million bucks.

00:03:09.962 --> 00:03:10.795
Right.

00:03:10.795 --> 00:03:11.628
Like I mean,

00:03:11.628 --> 00:03:13.150
and look what it's become.

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.761
The landscape in the
backyard is worth $2 million.

00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:17.193
You know what I mean?

00:03:17.193 --> 00:03:18.026
It's true.

00:03:18.026 --> 00:03:18.859
Right.

00:03:18.859 --> 00:03:19.830
It's crazy.

00:03:19.830 --> 00:03:21.218
We bought the company,

00:03:21.218 --> 00:03:24.102
and this wasn't allowed on pay-per-view.

00:03:24.102 --> 00:03:27.927
Porn was on pay-per-view
and you could pay for it,

00:03:27.927 --> 00:03:30.237
but you could not pay for the UFC.

00:03:30.237 --> 00:03:33.440
We bought the company and our
goal was to get it on free TV,

00:03:33.440 --> 00:03:36.507
which everybody thought
was impossible at the time.

00:03:36.507 --> 00:03:38.091
'Cause it was illegal.

00:03:38.091 --> 00:03:39.873
Yeah in some states.

00:03:39.873 --> 00:03:40.706
In some states.

00:03:40.706 --> 00:03:42.447
Yeah, it was illegal in some states.

00:03:45.848 --> 00:03:47.380
In fact as of 2001,

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.971
only two states sanctioned UFC fights.

00:03:49.971 --> 00:03:51.819
But after a lot of investment,

00:03:51.819 --> 00:03:53.799
and a lot of visits to state capitals,

00:03:53.799 --> 00:03:56.604
not only does all of North
America sanction fights,

00:03:56.604 --> 00:04:00.632
but the UFC broadcast to more
than 900 million households,

00:04:00.632 --> 00:04:02.382
all around the world.

00:04:06.141 --> 00:04:06.974
The growth of the company,

00:04:06.974 --> 00:04:09.291
and the sport is in large
part because of Dana.

00:04:09.291 --> 00:04:11.668
But also that the UFC is
set up much differently,

00:04:11.668 --> 00:04:14.466
than other pro sports
like the NFL or the NBA.

00:04:14.466 --> 00:04:18.549
So what makes you
different from Adam Silva,

00:04:18.549 --> 00:04:20.037
or Roger Goodell?

00:04:20.037 --> 00:04:22.081
I think the big difference
in what makes us,

00:04:22.081 --> 00:04:23.534
I wouldn't say better,

00:04:23.534 --> 00:04:25.893
but easier to manage than those things.

00:04:25.893 --> 00:04:28.922
There's one guy that makes all
the decisions and that's me.

00:04:28.922 --> 00:04:30.003
Yeah.

00:04:30.003 --> 00:04:32.528
I make all the decisions, you know?

00:04:32.528 --> 00:04:36.189
When I want to do
something, we're doing it.

00:04:39.347 --> 00:04:40.618
Unlike many other sports leagues,

00:04:40.618 --> 00:04:41.451
that have team owners,

00:04:41.451 --> 00:04:42.284
players,

00:04:42.284 --> 00:04:43.117
unions,

00:04:43.117 --> 00:04:44.328
or governing bodies who
weigh in on decisions,

00:04:44.328 --> 00:04:46.030
the UFC well,

00:04:46.030 --> 00:04:47.027
it has Dana.

00:04:47.027 --> 00:04:48.912
That's allowed him to be aggressive,

00:04:48.912 --> 00:04:50.575
over the last 20 years of business.

00:04:50.575 --> 00:04:52.243
And especially through the pandemic.

00:04:52.243 --> 00:04:53.828
In the United States,

00:04:53.828 --> 00:04:55.851
the UFC was the first
major sporting event,

00:04:55.851 --> 00:04:57.193
to resume operations.

00:04:57.193 --> 00:05:00.360
When it hosted UFC 249 in May of 2020.

00:05:01.613 --> 00:05:04.120
Tonight the first major US sporting event,

00:05:04.120 --> 00:05:05.322
since the COVID-19 shutdowns,

00:05:05.322 --> 00:05:07.685
will take place right
here in Jacksonville.

00:05:07.685 --> 00:05:09.742
Getting international fighters,

00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:13.019
into the octagon proved
to be more challenging.

00:05:13.019 --> 00:05:14.595
But Dana had an idea for that as well.

00:05:14.595 --> 00:05:17.818
The UFC is apparently building a facility,

00:05:17.818 --> 00:05:20.242
on a private island that
they're calling "Fight Island".

00:05:20.242 --> 00:05:22.253
Now is that's a clever name?

00:05:22.253 --> 00:05:23.086
No.

00:05:23.086 --> 00:05:24.296
Is it the perfect name?

00:05:24.296 --> 00:05:25.682
Yes.

00:05:25.682 --> 00:05:28.492
[Lawrence Epstein] That
started with Dana saying,

00:05:28.492 --> 00:05:29.861
I've got an idea.

00:05:29.861 --> 00:05:32.021
I want to buy my own private island.

00:05:32.021 --> 00:05:33.339
I want to own it myself.

00:05:33.339 --> 00:05:34.696
I want to set all the rules.

00:05:34.696 --> 00:05:36.839
I can do anything I
want to do on my island,

00:05:36.839 --> 00:05:39.910
and we're going to put
fights on on that island.

00:05:39.910 --> 00:05:41.775
We're not going to have
to listen to anybody,

00:05:41.775 --> 00:05:44.002
'cause it's going to be my island.

00:05:44.002 --> 00:05:45.058
This is Lawrence Epstein,

00:05:45.058 --> 00:05:46.671
UFC COO.

00:05:46.671 --> 00:05:48.191
And often when Dana has an idea,

00:05:48.191 --> 00:05:52.533
he's one of the people tasked
to turn it into a reality.

00:05:52.533 --> 00:05:53.492
And sort of my response was,

00:05:53.492 --> 00:05:54.372
"Okay Dana,

00:05:54.372 --> 00:05:55.229
I'm not sure that's going to work."

00:05:55.229 --> 00:05:56.062
Yeah.

00:05:56.062 --> 00:05:56.895
"But you know,

00:05:56.895 --> 00:05:58.226
there's gotta be an
opportunity for us out there."

00:05:58.226 --> 00:05:59.379
And ultimately we put on,

00:05:59.379 --> 00:06:01.341
these series of events in Yas island.

00:06:01.341 --> 00:06:03.899
And so it all started
with a crazy idea of Dana.

00:06:03.899 --> 00:06:05.147
Like I'm literally going to buy an island,

00:06:05.147 --> 00:06:06.638
I'm going to own it.

00:06:06.638 --> 00:06:07.471
Right.

00:06:07.471 --> 00:06:08.304
I'm going to be the king of that island.

00:06:08.304 --> 00:06:11.054
And I'm gonna do whatever I want.

00:06:13.556 --> 00:06:14.924
Keeping fights going during the pandemic,

00:06:14.924 --> 00:06:16.526
was important to Dana White.

00:06:16.526 --> 00:06:19.360
Critics and health officials
warned against matches.

00:06:19.360 --> 00:06:22.000
At one point even ESPN's
parent company Disney,

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:24.028
had to step in when the UFC sought,

00:06:24.028 --> 00:06:25.708
to avoid California state guidelines,

00:06:25.708 --> 00:06:28.003
by holding the event on tribal lands.

00:06:28.003 --> 00:06:29.950
But at a time when most other sports,

00:06:29.950 --> 00:06:31.599
had been almost entirely shut down,

00:06:31.599 --> 00:06:34.191
UFC was able to produce
matches for their fighters,

00:06:34.191 --> 00:06:37.257
and deliver on their contract with ESPN.

00:06:37.257 --> 00:06:39.653
It's one of the things
I'm the most proud of,

00:06:39.653 --> 00:06:42.177
out of my whole 20 year
career with the UFC,

00:06:42.177 --> 00:06:44.405
is that we didn't lay
off any of our employees.

00:06:44.405 --> 00:06:46.352
And we honored all our fighter contracts.

00:06:46.352 --> 00:06:47.868
And you know,

00:06:47.868 --> 00:06:50.426
everybody made a living
and got paid through COVID.

00:06:54.107 --> 00:06:55.361
Since the UFC,

00:06:55.361 --> 00:06:56.861
resumed live events in May of 2020,

00:06:56.861 --> 00:07:00.641
they've conducted about 55,000
tests of athletes and staff,

00:07:00.641 --> 00:07:03.974
with a positivity rate of about 1%.

00:07:05.796 --> 00:07:06.977
But as vaccines rolled
out through the country,

00:07:06.977 --> 00:07:08.756
and restrictions began to ease,

00:07:08.756 --> 00:07:11.500
the UFC was ready to bring fans back.

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:15.029
And in "Sin City" they
wanted it back in a big way.

00:07:15.029 --> 00:07:17.075
UFC president Dana White said,

00:07:17.075 --> 00:07:19.715
that Connor McGregor versus Dustin Poirier

00:07:19.715 --> 00:07:22.786
is happening July 10th
at the "T-Mobile" arena,

00:07:22.786 --> 00:07:23.956
at full capacity.

00:07:23.956 --> 00:07:25.606
We're here for UFC 264.

00:07:25.606 --> 00:07:27.256
And for the first time,

00:07:27.256 --> 00:07:28.510
since the start of the pandemic,

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:29.945
Las Vegas has sold out,

00:07:29.945 --> 00:07:31.561
the news up and down the strip.

00:07:35.087 --> 00:07:36.290
Vegas was alive again with activity.

00:07:36.290 --> 00:07:38.288
Thanks in large part to
the main event match,

00:07:38.288 --> 00:07:40.206
between Connor McGregor
and Dustin Poirier.

00:07:40.206 --> 00:07:42.648
And despite rising cases in Nevada,

00:07:42.648 --> 00:07:44.874
and the rise of the Delta
variant around the country,

00:07:44.874 --> 00:07:47.019
fans couldn't wait to be back.

00:07:47.019 --> 00:07:47.852
In fact,

00:07:47.852 --> 00:07:51.126
T-Mobile arena sold out
it's more than 20,000 seats,

00:07:51.126 --> 00:07:52.332
in just seconds.

00:07:52.332 --> 00:07:53.716
What's up everybody?

00:07:53.716 --> 00:07:54.549
How are ya?

00:07:57.467 --> 00:07:58.321
This was of course,

00:07:58.321 --> 00:07:59.492
back in July.

00:07:59.492 --> 00:08:01.590
And you may remember the
actual match ended up,

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:02.531
not going past the first round,

00:08:02.531 --> 00:08:05.088
after Connor McGregor suffered
a gruesome leg injury.

00:08:05.088 --> 00:08:06.922
But for the sport of combat fighting,

00:08:06.922 --> 00:08:08.652
it's never been more successful.

00:08:08.652 --> 00:08:10.695
I mean this isn't even the event.

00:08:10.695 --> 00:08:12.581
It's a press conference.

00:08:12.581 --> 00:08:13.916
Do you respect Dustin Poirier,

00:08:13.916 --> 00:08:16.107
no matter what happens on Saturday night?

00:08:16.107 --> 00:08:17.613
I don't give a about him,

00:08:17.613 --> 00:08:18.446
to be honest.

00:08:18.446 --> 00:08:22.093
I don't give a rat's ass about him.

00:08:22.093 --> 00:08:23.254
You've got your diehard fans.

00:08:23.254 --> 00:08:25.364
A lot of them were
sitting out there today.

00:08:25.364 --> 00:08:26.574
How do you get to the,

00:08:26.574 --> 00:08:28.824
the more casual sports fan?

00:08:30.688 --> 00:08:31.521
You know,

00:08:31.521 --> 00:08:33.706
I consider myself a pretty big sports fan,

00:08:33.706 --> 00:08:36.465
but candidly I've never
been a huge UFC fan.

00:08:36.465 --> 00:08:37.399
How do you get to me?

00:08:37.399 --> 00:08:38.232
Yeah.

00:08:38.232 --> 00:08:41.090
So what happens is through the pandemic,

00:08:41.090 --> 00:08:42.392
obviously we gained a lot of fans,

00:08:42.392 --> 00:08:43.863
because we were the only thing on TV.

00:08:43.863 --> 00:08:45.529
People tuned in people watched.

00:08:45.529 --> 00:08:46.934
We gained a lot of fans,

00:08:46.934 --> 00:08:48.584
because there was nothing to gamble on.

00:08:48.584 --> 00:08:50.626
So Sports Better started betting on UFC.

00:08:50.626 --> 00:08:52.742
And if you're going to watch UFC,

00:08:52.742 --> 00:08:54.651
you're going to end up loving it.

00:08:54.651 --> 00:08:56.894
There's no way that isn't exciting to you,

00:08:56.894 --> 00:08:58.215
and not fun to watch.

00:09:02.059 --> 00:09:02.892
And now in year three,

00:09:02.892 --> 00:09:04.330
of their seven year deal with ESPN,

00:09:04.330 --> 00:09:06.642
more and more people than
ever are being exposed to UFC,

00:09:06.642 --> 00:09:08.479
and MMA fighting.

00:09:08.479 --> 00:09:11.396
The UFC on ESPN.

00:09:15.678 --> 00:09:16.773
You think you want to be on ESPN.

00:09:16.773 --> 00:09:18.339
You think that's where you need to be.

00:09:18.339 --> 00:09:19.334
You're a sport.

00:09:19.334 --> 00:09:23.228
You don't really realize the
impact until you get on ESPN.

00:09:23.228 --> 00:09:24.061
Yeah.

00:09:24.061 --> 00:09:25.305
The impact has been massive.

00:09:25.305 --> 00:09:26.343
Tell me about that.

00:09:26.343 --> 00:09:27.760
Like in what way?

00:09:28.768 --> 00:09:30.228
Turn your TV on at three
o'clock in the afternoon,

00:09:30.228 --> 00:09:32.972
three o'clock in the morning, 6:00 AM.

00:09:32.972 --> 00:09:33.830
That bug is up there that says,

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.419
"Connor McGregor versus Poirier".

00:09:36.419 --> 00:09:39.213
Every single week that's up there.

00:09:39.213 --> 00:09:42.298
And these fighters names start
to drill into people's heads.

00:09:42.298 --> 00:09:45.051
You do that over a seven year period.

00:09:45.051 --> 00:09:46.226
It's massive.

00:09:46.226 --> 00:09:47.676
Yeah.

00:09:47.676 --> 00:09:48.908
Not just for the brand,

00:09:48.908 --> 00:09:50.627
but for the individual fighters too.

00:09:50.627 --> 00:09:53.267
The UFC is also important to ESPN,

00:09:53.267 --> 00:09:55.295
in an age of cord cutting,

00:09:55.295 --> 00:09:57.042
ESPN is looking to grow,

00:09:57.042 --> 00:09:59.171
their "ESPN Plus" streaming audience.

00:09:59.171 --> 00:10:00.408
It's a different day,

00:10:00.408 --> 00:10:01.992
and time with this younger generation.

00:10:01.992 --> 00:10:03.431
They're all cord cutters.

00:10:03.431 --> 00:10:04.451
And we have,

00:10:04.451 --> 00:10:06.497
not only do we have great content,

00:10:06.497 --> 00:10:07.787
and a massive fan base,

00:10:07.787 --> 00:10:10.176
now that we built over the last 20 years,

00:10:10.176 --> 00:10:11.579
to finally get to ESPN.

00:10:11.579 --> 00:10:15.177
Where we can actually add value to them,

00:10:15.177 --> 00:10:19.335
and our demographic are the cord cutters.

00:10:19.335 --> 00:10:20.168
Right.

00:10:20.168 --> 00:10:23.891
[UFC Ring Presenter] The UFC
Lightweight Championship,

00:10:23.891 --> 00:10:24.974
of the World.

00:10:26.671 --> 00:10:28.788
But the road to ESPN 20 years ago,

00:10:28.788 --> 00:10:30.491
for the UFC sounded laughable.

00:10:30.491 --> 00:10:31.324
Dana,

00:10:31.324 --> 00:10:32.649
congratulations on your first show.

00:10:32.649 --> 00:10:33.509
That's gotta feel good.

00:10:33.509 --> 00:10:35.080
Thank you very much James.

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:35.969
I appreciate it.

00:10:35.969 --> 00:10:37.206
We're very excited.

00:10:37.206 --> 00:10:38.499
After years of investment,

00:10:38.499 --> 00:10:39.949
in just making the sport legal,

00:10:39.949 --> 00:10:41.937
they still needed a way
to grow their audience.

00:10:46.971 --> 00:10:48.968
So they did what anyone in
the early 2000's would do.

00:10:48.968 --> 00:10:51.621
They started a reality show.

00:10:51.621 --> 00:10:52.928
We picked who we believe,

00:10:52.928 --> 00:10:53.761
are the best guys in
this country right now.

00:10:53.761 --> 00:10:55.749
Do you want to be a fighter?

00:10:55.749 --> 00:10:58.164
That's the question.

00:10:58.164 --> 00:10:59.088
When you look at every metric,

00:10:59.088 --> 00:11:00.809
every single metric relating to the UFC.

00:11:00.809 --> 00:11:01.642
Whether it's number of fans,

00:11:01.642 --> 00:11:02.758
profitability,

00:11:02.758 --> 00:11:03.746
ratings,

00:11:03.746 --> 00:11:04.579
pay-per-view buys.

00:11:04.579 --> 00:11:05.825
There's this inflection point.

00:11:05.825 --> 00:11:07.096
And that inflection point,

00:11:07.096 --> 00:11:08.350
is the "Ultimate Fighter" reality show.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:11.350
It was ruled a unanimous decision.

00:11:14.021 --> 00:11:15.395
To Josh Koscheck.

00:11:16.811 --> 00:11:19.270
Fight TV starts "Television
Network for Men".

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:21.286
We pitched "The Ultimate Fighter" to them,

00:11:21.286 --> 00:11:24.339
and they want nothing to do with it.

00:11:24.339 --> 00:11:25.567
So we say to them,

00:11:25.567 --> 00:11:27.467
"Well what if we pay for it?""

00:11:27.467 --> 00:11:28.756
They liked that idea a lot.

00:11:28.756 --> 00:11:29.589
Yeah.

00:11:33.838 --> 00:11:35.019
The last thing you want to do,

00:11:35.019 --> 00:11:37.085
is get kicked off the show.

00:11:37.085 --> 00:11:39.282
The UFC would put $10 million,

00:11:39.282 --> 00:11:41.733
into creating the first
season of the show.

00:11:41.733 --> 00:11:43.315
We all have to drink equally.

00:11:43.315 --> 00:11:46.204
Dana oversaw the production himself,

00:11:46.204 --> 00:11:47.954
and starred in the show.

00:11:47.954 --> 00:11:49.424
I don't want you here.

00:11:49.424 --> 00:11:51.650
And I'll throw you the out of this gym,

00:11:51.650 --> 00:11:53.402
so fast your head will spin.

00:11:56.402 --> 00:11:57.239
That paid off.

00:11:57.239 --> 00:11:58.431
And the ultimate fighter would go on,

00:11:58.431 --> 00:11:59.936
to be one of the biggest
draws for the network,

00:11:59.936 --> 00:12:01.832
and run for 14 seasons.

00:12:01.832 --> 00:12:03.777
And from the popularity of the show,

00:12:03.777 --> 00:12:05.198
the UFC would only grow.

00:12:05.198 --> 00:12:07.438
They then moved to Fox sports,

00:12:07.438 --> 00:12:09.057
and help launch their FS1 channel.

00:12:09.057 --> 00:12:11.318
But it also helped connect Dana,

00:12:11.318 --> 00:12:12.935
with one of the world's best known agents.

00:12:12.935 --> 00:12:13.976
Ari Emanuel.

00:12:13.976 --> 00:12:15.672
Get James Cameron on the phone.

00:12:15.672 --> 00:12:16.568
Get Dana Gordon on the phone.

00:12:16.568 --> 00:12:19.058
If you're not familiar with Ari Emanuel,

00:12:19.058 --> 00:12:21.122
you might know the entourage
character of Ari Gold,

00:12:21.122 --> 00:12:23.036
that was based off of him.

00:12:23.036 --> 00:12:25.524
This is now the biggest
agency in the world.

00:12:25.524 --> 00:12:27.752
And I'm the head of it.

00:12:27.752 --> 00:12:29.438
He now runs Endeavor,

00:12:29.438 --> 00:12:32.421
a newly public entertainment juggernaut.

00:12:32.421 --> 00:12:35.180
We had come up with a research department,

00:12:35.180 --> 00:12:37.107
to look at ratings and
helps us sign people.

00:12:37.107 --> 00:12:38.572
Helps us keep shows on the air.

00:12:38.572 --> 00:12:41.001
Different from any other
agency at the time.

00:12:41.001 --> 00:12:43.474
And the guy comes in to me and he says,

00:12:43.474 --> 00:12:45.344
"Well here's the number on spike."

00:12:45.344 --> 00:12:46.177
I go,

00:12:46.177 --> 00:12:48.202
"Holy cow that's incredible."

00:12:48.202 --> 00:12:50.234
I'm doing the agent signing thing.

00:12:50.234 --> 00:12:51.799
I'm calling him every day.

00:12:51.799 --> 00:12:52.937
It's a long game.

00:12:52.937 --> 00:12:53.913
A year later,

00:12:53.913 --> 00:12:55.083
Dana calls me and says,

00:12:55.083 --> 00:12:59.492
"If you can get me a
meeting with HBO boxing,

00:12:59.492 --> 00:13:00.759
I'll sign with you."

00:13:00.759 --> 00:13:03.149
Now I'm a character on a show,

00:13:03.149 --> 00:13:03.982
right?

00:13:03.982 --> 00:13:07.425
On HBO I've done most of the programming.

00:13:07.425 --> 00:13:08.479
I was like,

00:13:08.479 --> 00:13:10.259
this is like simple.

00:13:10.259 --> 00:13:11.469
You're like this is the thing?

00:13:11.469 --> 00:13:12.309
This is the thing?

00:13:12.309 --> 00:13:14.685
I should've just gone through
with that 9 months ago.

00:13:14.685 --> 00:13:15.518
Right?

00:13:18.401 --> 00:13:19.653
As Ari explains that
meeting didn't go well,

00:13:19.653 --> 00:13:23.925
but White did end up signing
with Ari as a client.

00:13:23.925 --> 00:13:25.544
And then in 2016,

00:13:25.544 --> 00:13:27.868
when the Fertitta brothers
decided to sell the UFC,

00:13:27.868 --> 00:13:31.036
it would be Ari and Endeavor
who would ultimately,

00:13:31.036 --> 00:13:32.620
buy a controlling stake in the UFC,

00:13:32.620 --> 00:13:35.507
valuing the company at about $4 billion.

00:13:35.507 --> 00:13:39.105
Remember the UFC was
bought by the Fertittas,

00:13:39.105 --> 00:13:40.953
and Dana for about $2 million,

00:13:40.953 --> 00:13:42.784
roughly 15 years earlier.

00:13:42.784 --> 00:13:44.615
When you jump out of bed,

00:13:44.615 --> 00:13:45.903
you better be ready to fight.

00:13:45.903 --> 00:13:47.289
You better be ready to kick ass and win.

00:13:47.289 --> 00:13:49.221
And since the sale Ari,

00:13:49.221 --> 00:13:51.757
and Endeavor have used the
whole of the company's portfolio

00:13:51.757 --> 00:13:53.872
to help grow the UFC even more.

00:13:53.872 --> 00:13:55.852
When you think about,

00:13:55.852 --> 00:13:58.593
and we can do this on many things,

00:13:58.593 --> 00:14:00.934
we call it inside the
company architecture,

00:14:00.934 --> 00:14:04.086
how we take elements of the portfolio,

00:14:04.086 --> 00:14:07.732
and use other elements to build
value across the platform.

00:14:07.732 --> 00:14:11.744
And if you think about
where we started at the UFC,

00:14:11.744 --> 00:14:13.641
when we got it to where it is now,

00:14:13.641 --> 00:14:17.073
that's only because of the
architectural platform,

00:14:17.073 --> 00:14:18.045
of the company.

00:14:18.045 --> 00:14:19.004
International sales,

00:14:19.004 --> 00:14:19.862
gambling,

00:14:19.862 --> 00:14:20.984
licensing,

00:14:20.984 --> 00:14:22.221
video games.

00:14:22.221 --> 00:14:25.684
Today, we're gonna do the
cheeseburger crunch wrap.

00:14:25.684 --> 00:14:27.963
The non-scripted group in WME,

00:14:27.963 --> 00:14:30.255
just sold the show to Food Network.

00:14:30.255 --> 00:14:32.564
Four episodes with Dana.

00:14:32.564 --> 00:14:33.802
This is so good!

00:14:33.802 --> 00:14:36.112
And that's going to expand our audience.

00:14:36.112 --> 00:14:38.250
So that's the architecture
of the business.

00:14:38.250 --> 00:14:39.926
Constantly adding value,

00:14:39.926 --> 00:14:40.881
adding audience,

00:14:40.881 --> 00:14:42.597
growing market share,

00:14:42.597 --> 00:14:43.869
growing awareness.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:50.668
And while many aspects of Endeavor,

00:14:50.668 --> 00:14:51.969
suffered from the pandemic,

00:14:51.969 --> 00:14:54.231
Hollywood was essentially
closed for business.

00:14:54.231 --> 00:14:55.929
The UFC thrived,

00:14:55.929 --> 00:14:58.670
so much so that in April of 2021,

00:14:58.670 --> 00:15:01.324
they would buy out the
remainder of the UFC,

00:15:01.324 --> 00:15:03.356
from investment firms KKR and Silver Lake,

00:15:03.356 --> 00:15:06.776
as part of a plan to take Endeavor public.

00:15:06.776 --> 00:15:07.609
In fact,

00:15:07.609 --> 00:15:09.604
according to Ari,

00:15:09.604 --> 00:15:11.026
owning all of the UFC was critical,

00:15:11.026 --> 00:15:13.419
to convincing Wall Street
that his ambitions were sound.

00:15:13.419 --> 00:15:14.340
The next phase,

00:15:14.340 --> 00:15:18.177
continuing to take the
UFC business global.

00:15:18.177 --> 00:15:21.379
10% Of the UFC audience
is in the United States,

00:15:21.379 --> 00:15:23.703
90% is international.

00:15:23.703 --> 00:15:25.933
The economics are switched.

00:15:25.933 --> 00:15:27.977
90% of the economics is domestic.

00:15:27.977 --> 00:15:29.793
10% is international.

00:15:29.793 --> 00:15:30.626
Interesting.

00:15:30.626 --> 00:15:32.280
I think there's a couple
sports that are global.

00:15:32.280 --> 00:15:33.819
Soccer's global,

00:15:33.819 --> 00:15:35.865
basketball is of some extent,

00:15:35.865 --> 00:15:38.198
but this is for sure global.

00:15:49.354 --> 00:15:53.420
So this is where I spend
a majority of my day.

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:55.282
Basically me,

00:15:55.282 --> 00:15:57.095
one of my lawyers,

00:15:57.095 --> 00:15:59.391
and two of our matchmakers.

00:15:59.391 --> 00:16:01.979
We sit in this room most of the day,

00:16:01.979 --> 00:16:02.812
every day.

00:16:02.812 --> 00:16:04.720
These are the fights that we're building.

00:16:04.720 --> 00:16:06.651
This is all the parts of the world,

00:16:06.651 --> 00:16:08.249
that the fighters are coming from,

00:16:08.249 --> 00:16:09.833
and where we wanna go.

00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:11.104
And what we want to do.

00:16:17.174 --> 00:16:18.514
And finding rising talent,

00:16:18.514 --> 00:16:20.296
from around the world
makes a big difference,

00:16:20.296 --> 00:16:21.813
to the UFC business.

00:16:21.813 --> 00:16:23.379
When we go into these new markets.

00:16:23.379 --> 00:16:24.663
For instance,

00:16:24.663 --> 00:16:26.447
when Connor McGregor became a star,

00:16:26.447 --> 00:16:28.082
he ignited Europe.

00:16:28.082 --> 00:16:29.351
Weili Zhang,

00:16:29.351 --> 00:16:30.904
our Chinese world champion.

00:16:30.904 --> 00:16:32.371
When she became a champion,

00:16:32.371 --> 00:16:33.760
she ignited China.

00:16:33.760 --> 00:16:36.184
When you have somebody who looks like you,

00:16:36.184 --> 00:16:37.306
talks like you,

00:16:37.306 --> 00:16:39.248
and comes from where you come from,

00:16:39.248 --> 00:16:41.728
and they're looked at as
the baddest human being,

00:16:41.728 --> 00:16:42.683
on planet earth,

00:16:42.683 --> 00:16:45.079
you rally behind these people.

00:16:45.079 --> 00:16:46.037
Yeah.

00:16:46.037 --> 00:16:47.879
And it becomes big.

00:16:47.879 --> 00:16:49.333
And then eventually once you do this,

00:16:49.333 --> 00:16:50.506
you know,

00:16:50.506 --> 00:16:52.099
in different parts of the world,

00:16:52.099 --> 00:16:54.431
you've got a real global sport.

00:16:58.637 --> 00:16:59.470
Fighters have,

00:16:59.470 --> 00:17:01.163
and will always be the engine of the UFC.

00:17:01.163 --> 00:17:03.755
But if there is one
speed bump in the road,

00:17:03.755 --> 00:17:05.018
to UFC global domination,

00:17:05.018 --> 00:17:08.916
it may be the multi-billion
dollar antitrust lawsuit,

00:17:08.916 --> 00:17:12.335
it's currently facing
from former UFC fighters.

00:17:12.335 --> 00:17:14.460
We filed this case in December of 2014,

00:17:14.460 --> 00:17:19.131
on behalf of a group of
mixed martial arts fighters,

00:17:19.131 --> 00:17:20.384
who fought for the UFC.

00:17:20.384 --> 00:17:23.717
On our way over to the courthouse now.

00:17:25.224 --> 00:17:26.057
In broad terms,

00:17:26.057 --> 00:17:27.798
the case is an antitrust case

00:17:27.798 --> 00:17:29.945
where we're claiming that the UFC,

00:17:29.945 --> 00:17:32.040
is both a monopoly and monopsony,

00:17:32.040 --> 00:17:33.888
meaning it is a dominant seller,

00:17:33.888 --> 00:17:35.705
of mixed martial arts services,

00:17:35.705 --> 00:17:39.037
and a dominant buyer of
mixed martial arts services.

00:17:39.037 --> 00:17:41.530
The lawsuit claims the UFC quote,

00:17:41.530 --> 00:17:44.762
"Engaged in an illegal scheme
to eliminate competition",

00:17:44.762 --> 00:17:47.271
and that allows it to pay fighters",

00:17:47.271 --> 00:17:48.104
quote,

00:17:48.104 --> 00:17:49.760
"A fraction of what they would earn

00:17:49.760 --> 00:17:51.588
in competitive marketplace."

00:17:51.588 --> 00:17:53.964
And then it has used
those tactics to bad ends,

00:17:53.964 --> 00:17:57.716
including suppressing the
compensation of the UFC fighters,

00:17:57.716 --> 00:18:01.214
and making it difficult for
fighters to get free agency,

00:18:01.214 --> 00:18:03.735
and have mobility and
control their own careers.

00:18:03.735 --> 00:18:05.336
Maybe unsurprisingly,

00:18:05.336 --> 00:18:07.514
Dana white doesn't see it like that.

00:18:07.514 --> 00:18:09.107
We bought the company in 2001.

00:18:09.107 --> 00:18:12.447
We didn't start making money
till like six or seven,

00:18:12.447 --> 00:18:13.538
right?

00:18:13.538 --> 00:18:16.394
Ever since the day we bought the company,

00:18:16.394 --> 00:18:19.034
fighter pay has gone like this,

00:18:19.034 --> 00:18:21.885
and it's gone up even more
in the last five years.

00:18:21.885 --> 00:18:26.885
And it's going to go up even
more in the next five years.

00:18:26.964 --> 00:18:28.274
William Isaacson,

00:18:28.274 --> 00:18:29.299
a lawyer for the UFC,

00:18:29.299 --> 00:18:30.962
said in a statement to Bloomberg that,

00:18:30.962 --> 00:18:32.612
"Average fighter compensation has risen

00:18:32.612 --> 00:18:35.112
by over 600% since 2005."

00:18:36.163 --> 00:18:38.813
But according to the
plaintiffs in the case,

00:18:38.813 --> 00:18:40.928
while UFC fighter pay has increased,

00:18:40.928 --> 00:18:43.159
the percentage of revenue
fighters received,

00:18:43.159 --> 00:18:46.753
has remained fairly stable and around 20%.

00:18:46.753 --> 00:18:47.660
And what this analysis shows,

00:18:47.660 --> 00:18:50.577
is that if the UFC was competitive,

00:18:52.399 --> 00:18:55.219
and did not allegedly
violate the antitrust laws,

00:18:55.219 --> 00:18:58.136
it would pay its fighters 50%,

00:18:59.148 --> 00:19:01.602
or more of the revenues it's generated.

00:19:01.602 --> 00:19:03.254
Just like baseball,

00:19:03.254 --> 00:19:05.036
just like hockey,

00:19:05.036 --> 00:19:06.668
just like basketball.

00:19:06.668 --> 00:19:08.401
And if that were to happen,

00:19:08.401 --> 00:19:11.719
if instead of paying 20%
of the revenues generated,

00:19:11.719 --> 00:19:14.570
it paid 50% or more of
the revenues generated,

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:18.557
the fighters would have
made $1.6 billion more,

00:19:18.557 --> 00:19:19.892
during the period,

00:19:19.892 --> 00:19:20.975
2010 to 2017.

00:19:23.807 --> 00:19:25.193
Usually when you're facing,

00:19:25.193 --> 00:19:27.041
this kind of legal battle
you tend to stay quiet.

00:19:27.041 --> 00:19:28.031
But for Dana,

00:19:28.031 --> 00:19:31.375
he's not afraid of letting
you know just how he feels.

00:19:31.375 --> 00:19:33.209
We built an industry from nothing,

00:19:33.209 --> 00:19:35.603
where if you followed the lines,

00:19:35.603 --> 00:19:38.441
of how many people have benefited,

00:19:38.441 --> 00:19:40.175
and made money from this company.

00:19:40.175 --> 00:19:42.467
And we changed the pay structure,

00:19:42.467 --> 00:19:44.724
so that everybody makes money.

00:19:44.724 --> 00:19:46.357
Not just the top guys.

00:19:46.357 --> 00:19:48.803
In boxing, the top guys make millions,

00:19:48.803 --> 00:19:50.415
and everybody else starves.

00:19:50.415 --> 00:19:52.429
Everybody makes money here.

00:19:52.429 --> 00:19:53.687
Everybody makes a good living,

00:19:53.687 --> 00:19:57.942
and there's enough money to
reinvest back into the sport.

00:19:57.942 --> 00:19:59.492
Grow the sport and grow the brand.

00:19:59.492 --> 00:20:00.996
We're growing a real business.

00:20:00.996 --> 00:20:02.826
We're heading into this,

00:20:02.826 --> 00:20:05.879
this country where
everybody gets a trophy,

00:20:05.879 --> 00:20:07.463
and everybody should get this.

00:20:07.463 --> 00:20:08.467
And everybody should get that.

00:20:08.467 --> 00:20:09.857
When I leave,

00:20:09.857 --> 00:20:11.340
when I leave,

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:12.428
maybe it'll turn,

00:20:12.428 --> 00:20:14.012
this place will be left at the hyenas,

00:20:14.012 --> 00:20:15.573
and then come in and rip this thing apart.

00:20:15.573 --> 00:20:17.676
But as long as I'm here,

00:20:17.676 --> 00:20:19.509
it ain't gonna happen.

00:20:27.229 --> 00:20:29.688
I have a lawyer who does a lot-

00:20:29.688 --> 00:20:30.711
The lawsuit is likely to take years,

00:20:30.711 --> 00:20:31.734
to resolve.

00:20:31.734 --> 00:20:32.641
And for Dana,

00:20:32.641 --> 00:20:33.648
the best way to grow fighter pay,

00:20:33.648 --> 00:20:35.710
is to continue the mission
of growing the business.

00:20:35.710 --> 00:20:38.627
And making more money for everyone.

00:20:47.657 --> 00:20:49.439
It's a huge weekend for entertainment,

00:20:49.439 --> 00:20:50.522
in Las Vegas.

00:20:51.419 --> 00:20:53.795
A highly anticipated UFC fight,

00:20:53.795 --> 00:20:56.717
filling in the T-Mobile arena tonight.

00:20:56.717 --> 00:21:00.217
It's fight night in Vegas,

